  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Request Path",
      "items": [
        "Browser traffic enters through Nginx, the only publicly exposed port",
        "The Streamlit server calls the API over the internal Docker network directly, not through Nginx's own /api/ proxy path",
        "RAGEngine.answer() makes exactly one outbound network call: the Gemini generate(prompt) request"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Retrieval Pipeline",
      "items": [
        "The question is expanded with statute wording before either retriever runs, so plain-language queries still match legal phrasing",
        "Hybrid Search fuses FAISS semantic search with an in-memory BM25 keyword index by reciprocal rank fusion",
        "An optional cross-encoder reranker re-scores the fused candidates; if it fails to load at startup, the API falls back to RRF ranking only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust Boundaries & Resilience",
      "items": [
        "Everything except Nginx sits on a private Docker network with no public ingress",
        "GEMINI_API_KEY leaves the process only on the single Gemini call; no other component talks to a third party",
        "If Gemini errors or hits its quota, the API returns the retrieved statute sections directly instead of a written answer and flags the response as degraded rather than failing the request",
        "The raw corpus JSON files are read once at startup to confirm the FAISS index matches current data, not on every query"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
